From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:32:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm: adbe: Add a KMS driver for the Apple A9 display pipe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The iPad 5 (J71t) and the other A9 devices run on simpledrm, which
copies every frame into the boot framebuffer and has no vblank. The A9
display pipe has no coprocessor: iBoot leaves the pipe, the eDP link and
the panel running, and the pipe takes new plane parameters through its
ADP parameter FIFO.

Add a KMS driver that adopts the running 1536x2048 mode with one
XRGB8888 primary plane. A flip pushes the new base (and stride, when it
changes) as one parameter packet; the pipe holds it until the next frame
boundary and raises its "packet applied" status bit there, which
completes the flip. Vblank comes from the same interrupt. The driver
never programs timings, clocks or the link. Disabling the CRTC scans out
the boot framebuffer cleared to black. On probe it retires the
simple-framebuffer device, so simpledrm cannot take the scanout back.

The FIFO port and the layer registers sit at the same offsets as in the
H7 pipe driven by drivers/gpu/drm/adp; the A9 pipe is the ADBE of iOS's
AppleH8ADBE0 kext.

Device result on J71t: native eDP-1, fixed-mode flips 31/31.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 71a3dfd5 (J71t ledger 11.1, 11.2) and
 omarchy-ipad5 patches/display/round3; reduced to the validated paths:
 base packet commit and "next frame" token, without the commit/token
 module parameters, the round-4 GEM/CMA accounting and the debugfs
 state. The apple_adbe_drm.enable=0 parameter is dropped: the DT node's
 status decides whether the driver binds, simpledrm keeps the display
 otherwise. The display DART walk from hard-coded addresses is replaced
 by the plane base check (bypass gives base == the boot framebuffer's
 low 32 bits); the driver holds the disp0 and dp power domains while
 bound; the flip timer fallback is dropped (the 3-vblank fallback
 stays).]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
